  "articleBody": "When you're planning an interior paint job, it’s easy to get caught up in the excitement and overlook some details that can lead to headaches later. One big mistake folks often make is choosing paint based on brand name alone, rather than considering the actual paint grade. Different grades have different qualities, and the right one depends on your needs and budget. Another common pitfall is not clarifying who’s responsible for prep work and repairs. Will patching and sanding be part of the quote, or are those separate add-ons? Getting this straight upfront avoids surprises. Also, always confirm how your furniture and floors will be protected, and what the end-of-day cleanup routine looks like. You don't want to come home to a messy house after a day's work! Lastly, a weak written contract or an unclear scope can cause problems. Make sure your quote specifies exactly what areas are covered, the number of coats, and payment terms. Avoiding these common mistakes can save you stress, time, and money, ensuring your painting project goes smoothly and you get the results you're dreaming of. If you’re unsure about any of these steps, it’s a good idea to talk with a professional who can guide you through the process.",
